<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I71c659b8854d11bc62e1286cc11b1f3d2eb03078" commit="fa10db1d96dc3e398562ef01a42e00f9011ca9ef" commit_message="frecon: add vertical threshold for &quot;hi-res&quot; splash screen  We currently only account for horizontal screen resolution for determining &quot;hi-res&quot; screens (and using an enlarged set of images for the boot splash animation). This doesn't always get us a good result when the vertical dimension is larger than the horizontal dimension.  Let's just apply the same threshold for both horizontal and vertical resolution.  BUG=chromium:791715 TEST=boot-splash on scarlet  Change-Id: I71c659b8854d11bc62e1286cc11b1f3d2eb03078 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/806923 Commit-Ready: ChromeOS CL Exonerator Bot &lt;chromiumos-cl-exonerator@appspot.gserviceaccount.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="806923" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/frecon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/frecon" ref="refs/changes/23/806923/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8bbb46ed3b9fdea9891da7b8a93fb4b792954dec" commit="7d181ba6ae8cae59b748bc9adfb919a6f3aec473" commit_message="non -ff able Merge commit '59b6c16' into branch  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I8bbb46ed3b9fdea9891da7b8a93fb4b792954dec Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/807246 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="807246" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/infra/dummies/merge-sandbox" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/infra/dummies/merge-sandbox" ref="refs/changes/46/807246/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5c946f6f5048ad11b67b50e44a3cdf833bd00d3d" commit="bedc714b092284e24fb83e859e2b011eea9fd5e9" commit_message="chromeos-infra-puppet-pre-cq: Add Puppet Pre-CQ builder  Need to land build config before iterating on the test stage.  BUG=chromium:686315 TEST=None  Change-Id: I5c946f6f5048ad11b67b50e44a3cdf833bd00d3d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/777979 Commit-Ready: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="777979" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/79/777979/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7acc030184b76d6c38a729cb64658f71e376c819" commit="1c6cf371106278f35162ddd8c4c14defea44791b" commit_message="sn5s330: Clear interrupts and setup masks at init.  When the SN5S330 is powered initially, there will be certain events set that will assert its interrupt line.  As part of the initialization for this part, we should clear all the pending interrupts and setup the masks for the events that we care about.  This commit clears all interrupts at init time and masks all interrupts except for overcurrent condition for PP1.  BUG=b:69139844 BRANCH=None TEST=Flash zoombini; With nothing plugged in, verify that the interrupt line is deasserted at boot. TEST=Repeat the above test with a charger plugged in.  Change-Id: I7acc030184b76d6c38a729cb64658f71e376c819 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/783510 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="783510" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/10/783510/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3308d3b1c060d45262de4106fa8ded27461a603f" commit="09e1ade2ec48c99b15558152b399a518369ad8d4" commit_message="Add OmahaDevserver back to autotest libraries.  This Class was in use with autoupdate_EndToEndTest for years. It was removed when that test was moved to the devserver-on-dut model. Regular update tests can use the local devserver model.  However, for updating at OOBE we need a devserver instance that can survive a DUT reboot because: 1. This update reboots in the middle without user intervention 2. we will want to extend this test to reboot in the middle of the update and verify that it continues. (We never want users to be able to skip forced update).  We cannot use exisitng lab devservers because we need devservers with two extra flags: --critical_update and --host_log. The first ensures that deadline:now is set in the omaha response which trigger forced update. The second ensure we have update events to parse and verify. These two flags are not used to start lab devservers.  BUG=chromium:782828 TEST=None  Change-Id: I3308d3b1c060d45262de4106fa8ded27461a603f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/805054 Commit-Ready: David Haddock &lt;dhaddock@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Haddock &lt;dhaddock@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Haddock &lt;dhaddock@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="805054" owner_email="dhaddock@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/54/805054/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie073bcf3694111c7bad69d627ae6826485c2ee28" commit="5df5293552bb5583d7767bcbfa70547d47d39548" commit_message="[autotest] Remove suite:perf_v2  This suite only has one test remaining in it (platform_MemoryMonitor). That test creates very many timeseries which weren't particularly useful on a performance dashboard, and, hence the entire suite was de-scheduled from running in the lab.  In any case, the recommend way to track performance is now by tests running in the suite:bvt-perbuild.  Therefore, let's completely kill the vestiges of this suite.  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:791830 TEST=none  Change-Id: Ie073bcf3694111c7bad69d627ae6826485c2ee28 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/807638 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="807638" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/38/807638/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="10186.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>